Subject: [PATCH 4/7] server: adapt lifecycle and networking for WASIX

WASIX lacks the Unix process-control and signal-delivery behavior used by
mysqld. Keep the server in the foreground, reject chroot/identity switching,
use an internal atomic shutdown notification, and wake the listener out of
its blocked poll through a pipe in its poll set: a signal handler runs under
WASIX but does not interrupt poll(), and a loopback connection to the
configured port is not a reliable wake, since the listener need not be
reachable at that address and WASIX connect() reports no failure. Also avoid
dynamic component autoloading and the unavailable ppoll signal-wakeup path.

For 8.4, also guard the SIGTRAP si_code cases of the fatal signal handler
the way upstream already guards the rarer ones: WASIX libc leaves
TRAP_BRKPT and TRAP_TRACE undefined because WASI has no signals.

diff --git a/sql/conn_handler/connection_acceptor.h b/sql/conn_handler/connection_acceptor.h
index 4012fb1cf..88e70151e 100644
--- a/sql/conn_handler/connection_acceptor.h
+++ b/sql/conn_handler/connection_acceptor.h
@@ -81,5 +81,10 @@ class Connection_acceptor {
     Close the listener.
   */
   void close_listener() { m_listener->close_listener(); }
+
+#if defined(__wasm__)
+  /** Wake a WASIX listener blocked in poll() during server shutdown. */
+  void wake_listener() { m_listener->wake_listener(); }
+#endif
 };
 #endif  // CONNECTION_ACCEPTOR_INCLUDED
diff --git a/sql/conn_handler/socket_connection.cc b/sql/conn_handler/socket_connection.cc
index 2463f6aab..ca6a0d5be 100644
--- a/sql/conn_handler/socket_connection.cc
+++ b/sql/conn_handler/socket_connection.cc
@@ -896,6 +896,15 @@ void Mysqld_socket_listener::setup_connection_events(
 
   for (const auto &socket_element : socket_vector)
     add_socket_to_listener(socket_element.m_socket);
+
+#if defined(__wasm__)
+  /*
+    The wake pipe's read end goes last in the poll set, after the sockets, so
+    that the socket entries keep their indexes.
+  */
+  if (pipe(m_wake_pipe) == 0)
+    m_poll_info.m_fds.emplace_back(pollfd{m_wake_pipe[0], POLLIN, 0});
+#endif
 }
 
